 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:06:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: round private buffer sizes up to whole pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The preallocated-memory allocator marks b->size >> PAGE_SHIFT pages as
used, so the tail of a buffer whose size is not a multiple of the page
size is left free in the bitmap and can be handed out again. Today the
64 KiB alignment of every allocation hides it for the context buffers
(30 KiB, 2 MiB), but not for a buffer that ends just past a 64 KiB
boundary.

Round the page count up on allocation and release alike.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr.c
index b25ad2a37..5b078cc0d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ int s5p_mfc_alloc_priv_buf(struct s5p_mfc_dev *dev, unsigned int mem_ctx,
 			   struct s5p_mfc_priv_buf *b)
 {
 	unsigned int bits = dev->mem_size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
-	unsigned int count = b->size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+	unsigned int count = DIV_ROUND_UP(b->size, PAGE_SIZE);
 	unsigned int align = (SZ_64K >> PAGE_SHIFT) - 1;
 	unsigned int start, offset;
 
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ void s5p_mfc_release_priv_buf(struct s5p_mfc_dev *dev,
 {
 	if (dev->mem_virt) {
 		unsigned int start = (b->dma - dev->mem_base) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
-		unsigned int count = b->size >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+		unsigned int count = DIV_ROUND_UP(b->size, PAGE_SIZE);
 
 		bitmap_clear(dev->mem_bitmap, start, count);
 	} else {
